# i18n Rules for Rails

## Translation File Structure

### File Organization
- `config/locales/defaults/` : Common translations (common, placeholders, etc.)
- `config/locales/models/` : ActiveRecord model translations
- `config/locales/views/` : View-specific translations
- `config/locales/views/navigation/` : Navigation translations
- `config/locales/views/auth/` : Authentication translations

### Naming Conventions
- One file per model : `config/locales/models/project/en.yml`
- One file per view : `config/locales/views/projects/en.yml`
- Always create files in English AND French

## ActiveRecord Model Translations

### Standard Structure
```yaml
en:
  activerecord:
    models:
      project:
        one: "Project"
        other: "Projects"
    attributes:
      project:
        name: "Name"
        description: "Description"
        start_date: "Start date"
        end_date: "End date"
        # Pour les énumérations et statuts
        statuses:
          todo: "To Do"
          in_progress: "In Progress"
          done: "Done"
```

### French Translations
```yaml
fr:
  activerecord:
    models:
      project:
        one: "Projet"
        other: "Projets"
    attributes:
      project:
        name: "Nom"
        description: "Description"
        start_date: "Date de début"
        end_date: "Date de fin"
        statuses:
          todo: "À faire"
          in_progress: "En cours"
          done: "Terminé"
```

## View Translations

### Recommended Structure
```yaml
en:
  projects:
    index:
      new_project: "+ New Project"
      no_projects_yet: "No projects yet"
    form:
      edit_title: "Edit project"
      create_title: "Create a new project"
    card:
      no_planning_defined: "No planning defined"
    show:
      progress: "Progress"
      build_capacity: "Build Capacity"
```

### Avoid Redundancy
- Don't duplicate model translations in views
- Use `t('activerecord.attributes.project.name')` instead of redefining
- Use `t('common.cancel')` for common elements

## Pluralization

### Use Native I18n Pluralization
```yaml
en:
  projects:
    card:
      member:
        zero: "0 members"
        one: "1 member"
        other: "%{count} members"
```

```yaml
fr:
  projects:
    card:
      member:
        zero: "0 membre"
        one: "1 membre"
        other: "%{count} membres"
```

### In Views
```erb
<%= t('projects.card.member', count: project.members.count) %>
```

### French Pluralization Rules
- 0 = plural (0 membres)
- 1 = singular (1 membre)
- 2+ = plural (2 membres)

